Okay.

260
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:39,050
So an inhaler is basically a device that you use to put steroids in your lungs that will help you breathe.

261
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:44,670
So some people, when they're running or they're walking, they're very short of breath and they can't breathe.

262
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:51,060
Well, there's a problem with this, like asthma, and they need to breathe this little inhaler.

263
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:53,240
It's like a little tube.

264
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,380
I think you inhale medicine from this little tube.

265
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,560
Yeah.

266
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,160
So the medicine helps open up your passageways.

267
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:03,760
It helps you breathe and it's very important for some people.

268
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:10,240
But in the case of an illness, like your lungs are very congested, this helps you breathe on the short term.

269
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,360
Right.

270
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:17,550
So to clear up is to allow air or the movement of something within your body, usually, I think.

271
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,600
Right.

272
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,600
But to clear up isn't necessarily about air.

273
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:23,870
It's basically a way to say that it will make this problem go away.

274
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:27,160
To clear something up is to make the problem go.

275
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,160
Right.

276
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:33,710
So I guess if you get medicine from a doctor, he'll say, okay, this will help you clear up your throat.

277
00:12:34,310 --> 00:12:34,550
Right.

278
00:12:34,550 --> 00:12:40,690
Or if you have a problem with acne, maybe your doctor will give you some cream to help clear up your acne, make it go away.

279
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Clear up your skin.

280
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:42,310
Okay.

281
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:44,370
So a lot of great examples there.

282
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:55,160
Why don't we go back and listen to the dialogue one last time.

283
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:55,770
Good afternoon, Chloe.

284
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,160
I'm Dr. Evans.

285
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,050
What seems to be the problem?

286
00:12:58,520 --> 00:12:59,490
Hi, Dr. Evans.

287
00:13:00,050 --> 00:13:02,110
Thanks for seeing me on such short notice.

288
00:13:02,770 --> 00:13:07,370
When I woke up this morning, I had a really sore throat and a really bad cough.

289
00:13:08,170 --> 00:13:10,410
I think I'm coming down with the flu.

290
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:11,870
I see.

291
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:14,300
Yes, you do sound rather croaky.

292
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,480
Well, let's have a look, shall we?

293
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:19,920
Could you please open your mouth and say, ah?

294
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:20,560
Ah.

295
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,100
Good.

296
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:22,920
Yes.

297
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,440
Your tonsils are a little swollen and red.

298
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:24,960
How are your ears?

299
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:25,860
Blocked at all?

300
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,850
A little, actually.

301
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:31,090
My sinuses are a little blocked up as well.

302
00:13:31,750 --> 00:13:33,250
I really feel terrible.

303
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:34,650
Okay, Chloe.

304
00:13:34,930 --> 00:13:38,190
Can you please breathe in and out slowly for me while I listen to your chest?

305
00:13:41,330 --> 00:13:43,130
Wow, you really are all bunged up.

306
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:44,790
You don't sound too good at all.

307
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,470
Okay, I'm going to set you up with a bunch of antibiotics.

308
00:13:48,510 --> 00:13:52,770
You will need to take these orange pills twice a day and these blue pills every evening.

309
00:13:53,250 --> 00:13:56,790
You will also have to take this cough medicine three times a day after meals.

310
00:13:57,410 --> 00:14:02,750
Finally, I am giving you an inhaler to use every time you feel breathless, just to clear up your lungs.

311
00:14:03,570 --> 00:14:05,330
Whoa, so many drugs.

312
00:14:06,230 --> 00:14:08,110
Ah, I hate swallowing pills.

313
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:09,990
Am I able to go to work?

314
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,400
Absolutely not.

315
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,680
You are highly contagious.

316
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,960
You don't want to infect the rest of your co-workers, do you?

317
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:22,140
I recommend staying in bed for at least three days and drinking plenty of fluids so you don't get weak and dehydrated.

318
00:14:22,510 --> 00:14:24,910
You can catch up on all the latest TV shows and movies.

319
00:14:25,350 --> 00:14:25,710
Okay.

320
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:28,630
Would you mind writing me a doctor's note for work?

321
00:14:29,270 --> 00:14:31,710
Otherwise, they may think I'm faking it.

322
00:14:32,250 --> 00:14:34,150
Sure, no problem.

323
00:14:34,810 --> 00:14:35,290
Here you are.

324
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:37,470
Now, off home and away to bed.

325
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:39,950
If you have any questions, just give me a call.

326
00:14:40,490 --> 00:14:41,750
Feel better soon and take care.

327
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:43,030
Thanks doc.

328
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:44,010
Bye.

329
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:45,800
Bye.

330
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:58,000
All right, so talking about illnesses and being contagious, we mentioned this pink eye illness before.

331
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:09,360
So this is the colloquial way of saying conjunctivitis, which is, I don't know if anyone has ever gotten it, your eye gets very, very red for a prolonged period of time.

332
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:09,550
That's right.

333
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,010
And it itches a lot.

334
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,360
It itches.

335
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:19,270
And so already your eye is very red or very pink, like the name says, but you really want to scratch it and itch it and it's really hard not to.

336
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:20,800
Yeah.

337
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,250
And I think you treat it by means of some eye drops.

338
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:24,050
Yeah.

339
00:15:24,050 --> 00:15:24,970
And you have to wait.

340
00:15:25,310 --> 00:15:31,130
I actually had a very bad case of pink eye once that I couldn't just clear up with drops.

341
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:33,430
The doctor gave me some eye drops.

342
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:38,800
They were so strong that I put them in my eye and I can taste them.

343
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:39,800
Oh, wow.

344
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:40,800
Yeah.

345
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:44,740
So apparently, yeah, it's very strange and it wouldn't clear up.

346
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:51,320
So then I had to get some kind of like a clear gel put in my eye and my eye patched up for like two days.

347
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,320
Oh wow.

348
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,320
Yeah.

349
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,320
So I was running around with one eye.

350
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,320
It was crazy.

351
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:59,680
I've never had it, but I know that it's very, very contagious, like we were saying earlier.

352
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:08,220
And so if a student at a school gets pink eye, all the parents get very nervous because it's very, very likely that he or she will give it to another person.

353
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:09,360
Yeah.

354
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:12,720
Because, you know, kids, if you touch your eye and you touch someone else, all of a sudden they have this disease.

355
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:14,320
Exactly.

356
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,800
So, yeah, it's very common thing.

357
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:23,680
And I think with especially with kids, they always get all these things, pink eye, measles.

358
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:24,680
They get chickenpox.

359
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,680
Chickenpox.

360
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,320
A lot of different diseases.

361
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,800
We actually have a lesson on chickenpox.

362
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,200
You guys should check that one out.

363
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:35,600
But if you have any questions, any comments or any other doubts, please come to EnglishPod.com where we're there to answer them.

364
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:36,340
We'll see you there.

365
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:37,840
Bye.

366
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:45,270
Bye.
